{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787505368582,"sessionID":"ses_fd06f755cffevoqtwk45u3vUdj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-c3c5266a-d1aa-43c7-bea7-6e8545b40cf1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-tgb7Rp/checkout/eslint.config.mjs"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-tgb7Rp/checkout/eslint.config.mjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { defineConfig, globalIgnores } from \"eslint/config\";\n2: import nextVitals from \"eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals\";\n3: import nextTs from \"eslint-config-next/typescript\";\n4: \n5: const eslintConfig = defineConfig([\n6:   ...nextVitals,\n7:   ...nextTs,\n8:   // Override default ignores of eslint-config-next.\n9:   globalIgnores([\n10:     // Default ignores of eslint-config-next:\n11:     \".next/**\",\n12:     \"out/**\",\n13:     \"build/**\",\n14:     \"next-env.d.ts\",\n15:   ]),\n16: ]);\n17: \n18: export default eslintConfig;\n\n(End of file - total 18 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { defineConfig, globalIgnores } from \"eslint/config\";\nimport nextVitals from \"eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals\";\nimport nextTs from \"eslint-config-next/typescript\";\n\nconst eslintConfig = defineConfig([\n  ...nextVitals,\n  ...nextTs,\n  // Override default ignores of eslint-config-next.\n  globalIgnores([\n    // Default ignores of eslint-config-next:\n    \".next/**\",\n    \"out/**\",\n    \"build/**\",\n    \"next-env.d.ts\",\n  ]),\n]);\n\nexport default eslintConfig;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-tgb7Rp/checkout/eslint.config.mjs","text":"import { defineConfig, globalIgnores } from \"eslint/config\";\nimport nextVitals from \"eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals\";\nimport nextTs from \"eslint-config-next/typescript\";\n\nconst eslintConfig = defineConfig([\n  ...nextVitals,\n  ...nextTs,\n  // Override default ignores of eslint-config-next.\n  globalIgnores([\n    // Default ignores of eslint-config-next:\n    \".next/**\",\n    \"out/**\",\n    \"build/**\",\n    \"next-env.d.ts\",\n  ]),\n]);\n\nexport default eslintConfig;","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":18,"totalLines":18,"truncated":false}},"title":"eslint.config.mjs","time":{"start":1787505368559,"end":1787505368579}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The T2 style uses `if (!Array.isArray(runs)) { throw new TypeError(\"runs must be an array\"); }`. I'll follow this convention too.\n\nAlright, let's write four files.\n\n### 1. `run-explorer.mjs`\n\n```js\nexport const sampleRuns = Object.freeze([...]); // keep as-is\n\nfunction assertRunsArray(runs) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(runs)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"runs must be an array\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction compareIds(a, b) {\n  if (a.id < b.id) return -1;\n  if (a.id > b.id) return 1;\n  return 0;\n}\n\nfunction isKnownCost(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value);\n}\n\nfunction roundTo(value, places) {\n  const factor = 10 ** places;\n  return Math.round(value * factor) / factor;\n}\n\nexport function filterRuns(runs, filters) {\n  assertRunsArray(runs);\n  const { assistant = \"all\", outcome = \"all\" } = filters ?? {};\n  return runs.filter((run) => {\n    const assistantMatches = assistant === \"all\" || run.assistant === assistant;\n    const outcomeMatches = outcome === \"all\" || run.outcome === outcome;\n    return assistantMatches && outcomeMatches;\n  });\n}\n\nconst SORT_COMPARATORS = {\n  \"score-desc\": (a, b) => b.score - a.score || a.elapsedSeconds - b.elapsedSeconds || compareIds(a, b),\n  \"time-asc\": (a, b) => a.elapsedSeconds - b.elapsedSeconds || b.score - a.score || compareIds(a, b),\n  \"cost-asc\": (a, b) => {\n    const aKnown = isKnownCost(a.costUsd);\n    const bKnown = isKnownCost(b.costUsd);\n    if (aKnown && !bKnown) return -1;\n    if (!aKnown && bKnown) return 1;\n    if (aKnown) {\n      return a.costUsd - b.costUsd || b.score - a.score || compareIds(a, b);\n    }\n    return b.score - a.score || compareIds(a, b);\n  },\n};\n\nexport function sortRuns(runs, order) {\n  assertRunsArray(runs);\n  const compare = SORT_COMPARATORS[order]; // hmm, for non-string order, SORT_COMPARATORS[undefined] → undefined\n  if (typeof compare !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(`Unsupported sort order: ${String(order)}`);\n  }\n  return [...runs].sort(compare);\n}\n\nexport function summarizeRuns(runs) {\n  assertRunsArray(runs);\n  if (runs.length === 0) {\n    return { visibleCount: 0, passRatePct: 0, medianElapsedSeconds: 0, totalCostUsd: 0, costedRunCount: 0 };\n  }\n\n  const visibleCount = runs.length;\n  const passCount = runs.filter((run) => run.outcome === \"pass\").length;\n  const passRatePct = roundTo((passCount / visibleCount) * 100, 1);\n\n  const elapsed = runs.map((run) => run.elapsedSeconds).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const middle = Math.floor(elapsed.length / 2);\n  const median = elapsed.length % 2 === 1 ? elapsed[middle] : (elapsed[middle - 1] + elapsed[middle]) / 2;\n  const medianElapsedSeconds = roundTo(median, 6);\n\n  let totalCostUsd = 0;\n  let costedRunCount = 0;\n  for (const run of runs) {\n    if (isKnownCost(run.costUsd)) {\n      totalCostUsd += run.costUsd;\n      costedRunCount += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  totalCostUsd = roundTo(totalCostUsd, 6);\n\n  return { visibleCount, passRatePct, medianElapsedSeconds, totalCostUsd, costedRunCount };\n}\n```\n\nWait a sec, about `roundTo` for passRatePct — roundTo(66.666..., 1) = Math.round(666.6666...)/10 = 667/10 = 66.7. ✓\n\nOne concern: `roundTo(median, 6)` — the committed test expects median 20 (integer). roundTo(20,6) = 20. ✓ deepStrictEqual(20) — Number, 20 === 20 ✓.\n\nFor the committed test's totalCostUsd 0.06: roundTo(0.04+0.02, 6) → 0.06, verified in the analysis. ✓\n\nNext, the UI part. Also need to think about: should the UI init be a named export? Not required. Keep it internal with a guard.\n\nUI:\n\n```js\nconst DEFAULT_FILTERS = Object.freeze({ assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" });\nconst DEFAULT_SORT_ORDER = \"score-desc\";\n\nfunction formatUsd(value) {\n  return `$${value.toFixed(2)}`;\n}\n\nfunction formatSeconds(value) {\n  if (value === 0) return \"0 s\";\n  return `${roundTo(value, 2)} s`;\n}\n\nfunction outcomeText(outcome) {\n  if (outcome === \"pass\") return \"Pass\";\n  if (outcome === \"fail\") return \"Fail\";\n  return outcome;\n}\n\nfunction createRunCard(run) {\n  const card = document.createElement(\"li\");\n  card.className = \"run-card\";\n\n  const head = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  head.className = \"run-card-head\";\n\n  const identity = document.createElement(\"span\");\n  identity.className = \"run-identity\";\n\n  const assistant = document.createElement(\"strong\");\n  assistant.className = \"run-assistant\";\n  assistant.textContent = run.assistant;\n  identity.appendChild(assistant);\n\n  const model = document.createElement(\"span\");\n  model.className = \"run-model\";\n  model.textContent = run.model;\n  identity.appendChild(model);\n\n  const badge = document.createElement(\"span\");\n  badge.className = `run-outcome run-outcome--${run.outcome === \"pass\" ? \"pass\" : \"fail\"}`;\n  badge.textContent = outcomeText(run.outcome);\n\n  head.appendChild(identity);\n  head.appendChild(badge);\n  card.appendChild(head);\n\n  const stats = document.createElement(\"dl\");\n  stats.className = \"run-stats\";\n  appendStat(stats, \"Score\", String(run.score));\n  appendStat(stats, \"Elapsed\", formatSeconds(run.elapsedSeconds));\n  appendStat(stats, \"Cost\", isKnownCost(run.costUsd) ? formatUsd(run.costUsd) : \"Subscription\");\n  card.appendChild(stats);\n\n  const runId = document.createElement(\"code\");\n  runId.className = \"run-id\";\n  runId.textContent = run.id;\n  card.appendChild(runId);\n\n  return card;\n}\n\nfunction appendStat(list, label, value) {\n  const term = document.createElement(\"dt\");\n  term.textContent = label;\n  const detail = document.createElement(\"dd\");\n  detail.textContent = value;\n  list.append(term, detail);\n}\n```\n\nWait — in `run-outcome--${...}`, what if outcome is some other value? The fixture only has pass/fail, but for safety: if it's not pass, map to a neutral class. `run.outcome === \"pass\" ? \"pass\" : \"fail\"` — for an unknown outcome, the \"fail\" styling would be misleading. Use a neutral one: `run.outcome === \"pass\" ? \"pass\" : run.outcome === \"fail\" ? \"fail\" : \"unknown\"`. And CSS defines pass/fail/unknown (unknown = gray). Good.\n\nNext, init:\n\n```js\nfunction initRunExplorer() {\n  const assistantFilter = document.getElementById(\"assistant-filter\");\n  const outcomeFilter = document.getElementById(\"outcome-filter\");\n  const sortSelect = document.getElementById(\"sort-order\");\n  const resetButton = document.getElementById(\"reset-filters\");\n  const resultsList = document.getElementById(\"results-list\");\n  const emptyState = document.getElementById(\"empty-state\");\n  const statusRegion = document.getElementById(\"result-status\");\n  const visibleCountEl = document.getElementById(\"visible-count\");\n  const passRateEl = document.getElementById(\"pass-rate\");\n  const medianTimeEl = document.getElementById(\"median-time\");\n  const knownCostEl = document.getElementById(\"known-cost\");\n  const knownCostNoteEl = document.getElementById(\"known-cost-note\");\n\n  function currentFilters() {\n    return {\n      assistant: assistantFilter.value,\n      outcome: outcomeFilter.value,\n    };\n  }\n\n  function render() {\n    const visibleRuns = sortRuns(filterRuns(sampleRuns, currentFilters()), sortSelect.value);\n    const summary = summarizeRuns(visibleRuns);\n    const totalRuns = sampleRuns.length;\n\n    resultsList.replaceChildren(...visibleRuns.map(createRunCard));\n    const hasRuns = visibleRuns.length > 0;\n    resultsList.hidden = !hasRuns;\n    emptyState.hidden = hasRuns;\n\n    visibleCountEl.textContent = String(summary.visibleCount);\n    passRateEl.textContent = `${summary.passRatePct.toFixed(1)}%`;\n    medianTimeEl.textContent = formatSeconds(summary.medianElapsedSeconds);\n    knownCostEl.textContent = formatUsd(summary.totalCostUsd);\n    knownCostNoteEl.textContent = `from ${summary.costedRunCount} of ${totalRuns} runs · subscription runs excluded`;\n\n    statusRegion.textContent = hasRuns\n      ? `Showing ${visibleRuns.length} of ${totalRuns} sample runs`\n      : \"No sample runs match the current filters\";\n  }\n\n  function resetControls() {\n    assistantFilter.value = DEFAULT_FILTERS.assistant;\n    outcomeFilter.value = DEFAULT_FILTERS.outcome;\n    sortSelect.value = DEFAULT_SORT_ORDER;\n  }\n\n  for (const control of [assistantFilter, outcomeFilter, sortSelect]) {\n    control.addEventListener(\"change\", render);\n  }\n  resetButton.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    resetControls();\n    render();\n  });\n\n  resetControls();\n  render();\n}\n\nif (typeof document !== \"undefined\" && document.getElementById(\"results-list\")) {\n  initRunExplorer();\n}\n```\n\nHmm wait, one issue: `passRateEl.textContent = summary.passRatePct.toFixed(1)` — passRatePct is already rounded to the first decimal place; toFixed(1) gives \"66.7\". 100 → \"100.0\". Good, always one decimal place.\n\n`resultsList.replaceChildren(...visibleRuns.map(createRunCard))` — no problem.\n\nGuard: in the browser the element exists. In Node, `document` is undefined → skip. But note: `typeof document !== \"undefined\" && document.getElementById(...)` — in Node the first check is false so no problem.\n\nEdge case: `document.getElementById` on a `document` that doesn't have it? No, it's a real DOM document so no problem.\n\nAlso, \"Reset restores all filters and score sort\" — resetControls sets the sort to score-desc. ✓\n\n\"Changing any select updates the records and summary\" — change listener. ✓\n\nNow, the last line of the original file: \"// Implement browser rendering and interactions without external dependencies.\" — I'll replace this with the actual implementation.\n\n### 2. `index.html`\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Benchmark run explorer</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"./styles.css\" />\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./run-explorer.mjs\"></script>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main class=\"explorer\">\n      <header class=\"intro\">\n        <p class=\"intro-kicker\">Benchmark evidence</p>\n        <h1>Benchmark run explorer</h1>\n        <p class=\"intro-copy\">\n          Filter and sort a small set of <strong>sample</strong> benchmark runs to see\n          how each assistant performed. These are fixture records for interface work,\n          not final study results.\n        </p>\n      </header>\n\n      <section class=\"controls\" aria-label=\"Filter and sort controls\">\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"assistant-filter\">Assistant</label>\n          <select id=\"assistant-filter\" name=\"assistant-filter\">\n            <option value=\"all\">All assistants</option>\n            <option value=\"Codex\">Codex</option>\n            <option value=\"Claude Code\">Claude Code</option>\n            <option value=\"OpenCode\">OpenCode</option>\n          </select>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"outcome-filter\">Outcome</label>\n          <select id=\"outcome-filter\" name=\"outcome-filter\">\n            <option value=\"all\">All outcomes</option>\n            <option value=\"pass\">Pass</option>\n            <option value=\"fail\">Fail</option>\n          </select>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"sort-order\">Sort order</label>\n          <select id=\"sort-order\" name=\"sort-order\">\n            <option value=\"score-desc\">Score (high to low)</option>\n            <option value=\"time-asc\">Time (fastest)</option>\n            <option value=\"cost-asc\">Cost (known first)</option>\n          </select>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field field--actions\">\n          <span class=\"field-spacer\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n          <button type=\"button\" id=\"reset-filters\" class=\"reset-button\">Reset filters</button>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n      ...\n```\n\nHmm, about the button placement: for a clean grid: the controls are `grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)) auto;` with the button in the last cell aligned to the end. A label-less field with the button — for alignment: put a spacer. Or more simply: a 3-column grid with the button spanning? Let me try to make it simpler and more robust:\n\n.controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)) auto; gap: 1rem; align-items: end; }\n.field { display: grid; gap: .5rem; }\n.field--actions { display: grid; align-content: end; } — the button aligns to the bottom edge of the select (the select is below the label). With align-items: end on the grid, the button aligns to the bottom edge of the row. The select's height is the row's height (label + gap + select). A button with align-self:end aligns to the bottom edge of the row = the bottom of the select.\n\n@media (max-width: 720px): .controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .field--actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; } button full width. And at very small sizes, 1fr.\n\nSummary section:\n\n```html\n<section class=\"summary\" aria-label=\"Summary of visible runs\">\n  <div class=\"summary-card\">\n    <p class=\"summary-label\">Visible runs</p>\n    <p class=\"summary-value\" id=\"visible-count\">–</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"summary-card\">\n    <p class=\"summary-label\">Pass rate</p>\n    <p class=\"summary-value\" id=\"pass-rate\">–</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"summary-card\">\n    <p class=\"summary-label\">Median elapsed time</p>\n    <p class=\"summary-value\" id=\"median-time\">–</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"summary-card\">\n    <p class=\"summary-label\">Known cost total</p>\n    <p class=\"summary-value\" id=\"known-cost\">–</p>\n    <p class=\"summary-note\" id=\"known-cost-note\">Subscription runs have no known cost and are excluded.</p>\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n\nInitial \"–\" placeholder text — will be replaced on the first render. OK.\n\nStatus + results:\n\n```html\n<p class=\"result-status\" id=\"result-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n\n<section class=\"results\" aria-label=\"Visible benchmark runs\">\n  <ul id=\"results-list\" class=\"results-list\"></ul>\n  <p id=\"empty-state\" class=\"empty-state\" hidden>No runs match the current filters. Reset or widen the filters to see sample runs.</p>\n</section>\n```\n\nHmm wait: the regex for empty-state requires `id=\"empty-state\"[^>]+hidden`. My tag: `<p id=\"empty-state\" class=\"empty-state\" hidden>` ✓.\n\nBut note — the regex `assert.match(html, /id=[\"']reset-filters[\"']/i)` ✓. `aria-live=[\"']polite[\"']` ✓.\n\nFooter? Add a small footer note: \"Sample fixture data · T4 run explorer\". Optional; keep it minimal but nice: `<footer class=\"explorer-footer\"><p>Sample fixture records only — not final study results.</p></footer>`. The intro already says that. Skip the footer? A small footer adds polish. I'll include a short one.\n\nNow — the \"–\" initial content: no problem.\n\n### 3. `styles.css`\n\nLet me write the complete CSS:\n\n```css\n:root {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  --bg: #f3f4fa;\n  --surface: #ffffff;\n  --ink: #1f2430;\n  --ink-muted: #5a6172;\n  --line: #d8dbe6;\n  --accent: #2f5fe0;\n  --accent-strong: #1f46b4;\n  --accent-soft: #e8edfc;\n  --pass-bg: #e3f4e9;\n  --pass-ink: #14603a;\n  --fail-bg: #fbe9ea;\n  --fail-ink: #99252e;\n  --unknown-bg: #eceef4;\n  --unknown-ink: #454b5c;\n  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(31, 36, 48, 0.06), 0 8px 24px rgba(31, 36, 48, 0.07);\n  --radius: 12px;\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif;\n}\n\n* , *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--ink);\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.explorer {\n  max-width: 72rem;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 3.5rem;\n}\n\n/* intro */\n.intro-kicker {\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--accent-strong);\n}\n\n.intro h1 {\n  margin: 0 0 0.75rem;\n  font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 1.2rem + 2.4vw, 2.6rem);\n  line-height: 1.15;\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n}\n\n.intro-copy {\n  margin: 0;\n  max-width: 56ch;\n  color: var(--ink-muted);\n  font-size: 1.05rem;\n}\n```\n\nControls:\n\n```css\n.controls {\n  margin-top: 2rem;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)) auto;\n  gap: 1rem 1.25rem;\n  align-items: end;\n  padding: 1.25rem;\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: var(--radius);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n}\n\n.field { display: grid; gap: 0.45rem; }\n\n.field label {\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: var(--ink-muted);\n}\n\n.field select {\n  width: 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;\n  font: inherit;\n  color: var(--ink);\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: border-color 120ms ease, box-shadow 120ms ease;\n}\n\n.field select:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }\n\n.field select:focus-visible,\n.reset-button:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n}\n\n.reset-button {\n  padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #fff;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  border: 1px solid var(--accent);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background-color 120ms ease, transform 120ms ease;\n}\n\n.reset-button:hover { background: var(--accent-strong); }\n.reset-button:active { transform: translateY(1px); }\n```\n\nWait: focus-visible on the button: the outline is accent but the button's background is also accent — is a 3px outline with 2px offset on a white card visible? The outline is accent-colored on top of a white card — the button's fill is also accent, so the outline merges visually? The outline is drawn outside the border with a 2px gap of card-white, so it appears as a ring separated by white — it's visible. OK. Maybe I should use a darker ring color for the button: keep it simple.\n\nSummary:\n\n```css\n.summary {\n  margin-top: 1.25rem;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));\n  gap: 1rem;\n}\n\n.summary-card {\n  padding: 1rem 1.15rem;\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: var(--radius);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n}\n\n.summary-label { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }\n.summary-value { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.summary-note { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }\n```\n\nStatus:\n\n```css\n.result-status {\n  margin: 1.4rem 0 0.75rem;\n  font-size: 0.92rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: var(--ink-muted);\n}\n```\n\nResults:\n\n```css\n.results { min-width: 0; }\n\n.results-list {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  list-style: none;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 19rem), 1fr));\n  gap: 1rem;\n}\n\n.run-card {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 0.8rem;\n  padding: 1rem 1.15rem;\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: var(--radius);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n  transition: transform 140ms ease, box-shadow 140ms ease, border-color 140ms ease;\n}\n\n.run-card:hover {\n  transform: translateY(-2px);\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(31,36,48,.08), 0 14px 30px rgba(31,36,48,.12);\n}\n\n.run-card-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }\n\n.run-identity { display: grid; gap: 0.1rem; min-width: 0; }\n.run-assistant { font-size: 1.02rem; font-weight: 700; }\n.run-model { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }\n\n.run-outcome {\n  padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: 0.02em;\n}\n.run-outcome--pass { background: var(--pass-bg); color: var(--pass-ink); }\n.run-outcome--fail { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail-ink); }\n.run-outcome--unknown { background: var(--unknown-bg); color: var(--unknown-ink); }\n\n.run-stats {\n  margin: 0;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));\n  gap: 0.5rem;\n  padding-top: 0.8rem;\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);\n}\n\n.run-stats dt { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }\n.run-stats dd { margin: 0.15rem 0 0; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n\n.run-id {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n  color: var(--ink-muted);\n}\n\n.empty-state {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem;\n  text-align: center;\n  color: var(--ink-muted);\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px dashed var(--line);\n  border-radius: var(--radius);\n}\n```\n\nHmm — the `.run-stats` grid with 3 columns inside a ~19rem card: \"Elapsed 72.4 s\" wraps to two lines, that's fine, no page scroll (wrap ≠ scroll). OK.\n\nMedia queries:\n\n```css\n@media (max-width: 900px) {\n  .summary { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n  .controls { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n  .field--actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n  .reset-button { width: 100%; }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 720px) {\n  .explorer { padding: 1.75rem 1rem 2.5rem; }\n  .controls { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }\n  .field--actions { grid-column: auto; }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .summary { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }\n}\n\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .run-card,\n  .field select,\n  .reset-button {\n    transition: none;\n  }\n  .run-card:hover { transform: none; }\n}\n```\n\nCheck the regex: `@media\\s*\\([^)]*max-width\\s*:` — \"@media (max-width: 900px)\" → `[^)]*` = \" \" then `max-width:` ✓.\n\n`:focus-visible` ✓ appears.\n\nContrast check:\n- --ink-muted #5a6172 on white: contrast? Luminance of #5a6172: r=90,g=97,b=114 → relative luminance ≈ 0.116? Contrast against white ≈ (1.05)/(0.116+0.05) ≈ 6.3:1 ✓.\n- --pass-ink #14603a on #e3f4e9: dark green on light green — high contrast ✓ (about 7:1).\n- --fail-ink #99252e on #fbe9ea: about 6:1 ✓.\n- --accent-strong #1f46b4 on white about 8:1 ✓ (for the kicker).\n- White button text on #2f5fe0: contrast of #2f5fe0: r=47,g=95,b=224 → luminance ≈ 0.135? (0.2126*lin(47/255)+0.7152*lin(95/255)+0.0722*lin(224/255)). lin(0.184)=0.0284, lin(0.3725)=0.1144, lin(0.878)=0.7454. → 0.2126*0.0284 + 0.7152*0.1144 + 0.0722*0.7454 = 0.00604+0.08182+0.05382=0.1417. Contrast against white = 1.05/0.1917 = 5.48:1 ✓ (AA for normal text).\n\nGood.\n\nAlso \"at desktop widths, use horizontal space efficiently\" — summary in 4 columns, controls in a row, results auto-fill multi-column ✓.\n\n\"Controls and results must reflow without horizontal page scroll\" — all grids use minmax(0,1fr)/min(100%,...) and overflow-wrap; body has no fixed width ✓. Add `overflow-wrap: anywhere` where needed (dd). Long model names wrap.\n\n### 4. `student-tests.mjs`\n\n```js\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { filterRuns, sampleRuns, sortRuns, summarizeRuns } from \"./run-explorer.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"filterRuns rejects non-array input and honors 'all' wildcards\", () => {\n  assert.throws(() => filterRuns(null, { assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" }), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => filterRuns(\"runs\", { assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" }), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => filterRuns({ id: \"x\" }, { assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" }), TypeError);\n\n  const all = filterRuns(sampleRuns, { assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" });\n  assert.deepEqual(all.map((run) => run.id), sampleRuns.map((run) => run.id));\n  assert.notEqual(all, sampleRuns);\n});\n\ntest(\"filterRuns matches exact, case-sensitive values and combines both filters\", () => {\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    filterRuns(sampleRuns, { assistant: \"codex\", outcome: \"all\" }).map((r) => r.id),\n    [],\n  );\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    filterRuns(sampleRuns, { assistant: \"Claude Code\", outcome: \"fail\" }).map((r) => r.id),\n    [\"cc-fable-02\"],\n  );\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    filterRuns(sampleRuns, { assistant: \"OpenCode\", outcome: \"pass\" }).map((r) => r.id),\n    [\"oc-kimi-01\"],\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"filterRuns does not mutate the input array\", () => {\n  const input = [\n    { id: \"a\", assistant: \"Codex\", outcome: \"pass\" },\n    { id: \"b\", assistant: \"OpenCode\", outcome: \"fail\" },\n  ];\n  const before = JSON.stringify(input);\n  filterRuns(input, { assistant: \"Codex\", outcome: \"fail\" });\n  filterRuns(input, { assistant: \"all\", outcome: \"all\" });\n  assert.equal(JSON.stringify(input), before);\n});\n```\n\nWait — the sample data: assistant \"OpenCode\" with outcome pass → only oc-kimi-01 (oc-qwen-01 is fail). ✓. \"Claude Code\" + fail → cc-fable-02 ✓ (cc-fable-01 is pass). \"codex\" lowercase → [] ✓ (case-sensitive: \"Codex\" ≠ \"codex\").\n\n```js\ntest(\"sortRuns validates input and order\", () => {\n  assert.throws(() => sortRuns(\"nope\", \"score-desc\"), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => sortRuns(null, \"time-asc\"), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => sortRuns(sampleRuns, \"score-asc\"), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => sortRuns(sampleRuns, \"\"), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => sortRuns(sampleRuns, undefined), TypeError);\n});\n```\n\nHmm — `sortRuns(sampleRuns, undefined)`: `SORT_COMPARATORS[undefined]` → undefined → throws TypeError ✓.\n\n```js\ntest(\"sortRuns orders time-asc and cost-asc with tie-breaks\", () => {\n  const byTime = sortRuns(sampleRuns, \"time-asc\");\n  assert.deepEqual(byTime.map((run) => run.id), [\n    \"oc-qwen-01\",\n    \"oc-kimi-01\",\n    \"cx-sol-02\",\n    \"cx-sol-01\",\n    \"cc-fable-01\",\n    \"cc-fable-02\",\n  ]);\n\n  const byCost = sortRuns(sampleRuns, \"cost-asc\");\n  assert.deepEqual(byCost.map((run) => run.id), [\n    \"oc-qwen-01\",\n    \"oc-kimi-01\",\n    \"cc-fable-01\",\n    \"cx-sol-01\",\n    \"cx-sol-02\",\n    \"cc-fable-02\",\n  ]);\n});\n```\n\nVerify time-asc: elapsed: cx-sol-01 72.4, cc-fable-01 88.1, oc-kimi-01 45.2, oc-qwen-01 41.8, cc-fable-02 101.6, cx-sol-02 64.9. Ascending: 41.8 oc-qwen-01, 45.2 oc-kimi-01, 64.9 cx-sol-02, 72.4 cx-sol-01, 88.1 cc-fable-01, 101.6 cc-fable-02. ✓ No ties.\n\ncost-asc: known: oc-qwen-01 0.05, oc-kimi-01 0.14 → order is oc-qwen-01, oc-kimi-01. null: cc-fable-01 97, cx-sol-01 96, cx-sol-02 91, cc-fable-02 84 → score-desc: cc-fable-01, cx-sol-01, cx-sol-02, cc-fable-02. ✓ As per interpretation A.\n\n```js\ntest(\"sortRuns breaks full ties by lexicographic id\", () => {\n  const tied = [\n    { id: \"zeta\", assistant: \"A\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 90, elapsedSeconds: 12, costUsd: 1 },\n    { id: \"alpha\", assistant: \"B\", outcome: \"fail\", score: 90, elapsedSeconds: 12, costUsd: 1 },\n    { id: \"mid\", assistant: \"C\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 90, elapsedSeconds: 12, costUsd: 1 },\n  ];\n  assert.deepEqual(sortRuns(tied, \"score-desc\").map((r) => r.id), [\"alpha\", \"mid\", \"zeta\"]);\n  assert.deepEqual(sortRuns(tied, \"time-asc\").map((r) => r.id), [\"alpha\", \"mid\", \"zeta\"]);\n  assert.deepEqual(sortRuns(tied, \"cost-asc\").map((r) => r.id), [\"alpha\", \"mid\", \"zeta\"]);\n});\n```\n\nFor cost-asc with all costs equal (1,1,1): known vs known → cost diff 0 → score diff 0 → id. ✓.\n\nAlso verify sortRuns doesn't mutate:\n\n```js\ntest(\"sortRuns returns a new array without mutating input\", () => {\n  const input = [...sampleRuns];\n  const order = input.map((r) => r.id);\n  sortRuns(input, \"time-asc\");\n  assert.deepEqual(input.map((r) => r.id), order);\n});\n```\n\nsummarize tests:\n\n```js\ntest(\"summarizeRuns rejects non-array input and returns zeros for empty input\", () => {\n  assert.throws(() => summarizeRuns(undefined), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => summarizeRuns(42), TypeError);\n  assert.deepEqual(summarizeRuns([]), {\n    visibleCount: 0,\n    passRatePct: 0,\n    medianElapsedSeconds: 0,\n    totalCostUsd: 0,\n    costedRunCount: 0,\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"summarizeRuns handles even-count medians and avoids float residue\", () => {\n  const runs = [\n    { id: \"a\", assistant: \"A\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 80, elapsedSeconds: 1, costUsd: 0.1 },\n    { id: \"b\", assistant: \"B\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 70, elapsedSeconds: 3, costUsd: 0.2 },\n    { id: \"c\", assistant: \"C\", outcome: \"fail\", score: 60, elapsedSeconds: 5, costUsd: null },\n    { id: \"d\", assistant: \"D\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 50, elapsedSeconds: 7, costUsd: 0.05 },\n  ];\n  assert.deepEqual(summarizeRuns(runs), {\n    visibleCount: 4,\n    passRatePct: 75,\n    medianElapsedSeconds: 4,\n    totalCostUsd: 0.35,\n    costedRunCount: 3,\n  });\n});\n```\n\nVerify: passCount 3/4 = 75% → 75. Median of [1,3,5,7] → (3+5)/2 = 4 ✓. Cost 0.1+0.2+0.05 = 0.35000000000000003? 0.1+0.2 = 0.30000000000000004; +0.05 = 0.35000000000000003? → roundTo 6 → 0.35 ✓. costedRunCount 3 ✓. deepStrictEqual with 75 (number) — my passRatePct: roundTo(75, 1) = Math.round(750)/10 = 75 ✓ number.\n\nNote: `deepEqual` in strict mode checks `passRatePct: 75` — my value 75 ✓.\n\nAdd one more: mutation safety + a full-data summarize? The committed suite covers full-data summarize. Add:\n\n```js\ntest(\"summarizeRuns does not mutate the input array or records\", () => {\n  const runs = [\n    { id: \"a\", assistant: \"A\", outcome: \"pass\", score: 10, elapsedSeconds: 9, costUsd: 1.5 },\n    { id: \"b\", assistant: \"B\", outcome: \"fail\", score: 20, elapsedSeconds: 1, costUsd: null },\n  ];\n  const snapshot = JSON.stringify(runs);\n  summarizeRuns(runs);\n  assert.equal(JSON.stringify(runs), snapshot);\n  assert.deepEqual(runs.map((r) => r.id), [\"a\", \"b\"]);\n});\n```\n\nThat gives about 8 test cases — well above the \"at least 2\" requirement. All meaningful, no skips/todos.\n\nOne more check — `sortRuns` with `Object.freeze`d sampleRuns: `[...runs].sort(compare)` — sort only reorders the new array; the frozen records aren't modified ✓.\n\nAnd `filterRuns(sampleRuns, ...)` — filter creates a new array ✓.\n\nNow, the potential gotcha in my student test \"filterRuns does not mutate the input array\": JSON.stringify of the input after filterRuns — filter doesn't touch it ✓.\n\nNow, is `import { filterRuns, sampleRuns, sortRuns, summarizeRuns } from \"./run-explorer.mjs\";` — importing sampleRuns triggers top-level code — in Node `document` is undefined → guarded ✓.\n\nLet me double-check that `replaceChildren` with a spread of an empty array is fine: `replaceChildren()` with no args clears ✓.\n\nOne more HTML detail: the task says \"one main heading\" — exactly one h1 ✓. \"a short explanation that these are sample records, not final study results\" ✓ the intro-copy.\n\n\"Labeled native select\" — `<label for>` + `<select>` ✓. Options exactly as specified:\n- assistant-filter: \"All assistants\", \"Codex\", \"Claude Code\", \"OpenCode\" ✓\n- outcome-filter: \"All outcomes\", \"Pass\", \"Fail\" ✓\n- sort-order: \"Score (high to low)\", \"Time (fastest)\", \"Cost (known first)\" ✓\n\n\"Provide a `Reset filters` button with ID `reset-filters`\" ✓.\n\n\"Display four summary values with IDs `visible-count`, `pass-rate`, `median-time`, `known-cost`. Make it clear that unknown subscription costs are excluded.\" ✓ — note + label \"Known cost total\".\n\n\"Render visible records into `results-list`. Each record must visibly name the assistant, model, outcome text, score, elapsed seconds, and either a USD cost or `Subscription`.\" ✓.\n\n\"Concise result-count message in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region\" ✓.\n\n\"Include an `empty-state` that is hidden initially. When no records match, show it and leave the results list empty.\" ✓.\n\n\"Changing any select updates the records and summary\" ✓. \"Reset restores all filters and score sort\" ✓.\n\n\"Build the result markup with safe DOM APIs... don't assign record data through innerHTML.\" ✓ — only createElement/textContent/className. No innerHTML anywhere. Let me also double-check the HTML file has no inline `style=` — none.\n\nNow, about `formatSeconds` for a median of 0 (empty) — we don't render the summary when empty? Actually we do: when empty, the summary shows zeros: visible-count \"0\", pass-rate \"0.0%\", median \"0 s\", known-cost \"$0.00\". Fine.\n\nformatSeconds(0) → \"0 s\" ✓. formatUsd(0) → \"$0.00\" ✓.\n\n`formatSeconds(68.65)` → roundTo(68.65, 2) = 68.65 → \"68.65 s\" ✓.\n\nNow — one subtle point: `summary.passRatePct.toFixed(1)` — passRatePct is a number; even when rounded to 66.7, toFixed(1) → \"66.7\" ✓.\n\nEdge case: passRatePct 100 → \"100.0%\" ✓.\n\nAlright, let's write it all. One more point about the top-level guard in `run-explorer.mjs`: some test runners (node --test) load the file in an ESM context where `document` is undefined — no problem.\n\nAlso, should the UI init wait for DOMContentLoaded? The script is `type=\"module\"` in `<head>` — module scripts are deferred by default, so the DOM is parsed before execution. ✓ No need for DOMContentLoaded.\n\nNow let me also think about `resultsList.hidden = !hasRuns` — hiding a `<ul>` via the hidden attribute ✓. And `emptyState.hidden = hasRuns` ✓.\n\nI think there's one more requirement: \"at 720px or less, controls and results must reflow without horizontal page scroll.\" My results grid: `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 19rem), 1fr))` — at container width < 19rem, minmax(100%...) → 1 column = container width ✓ no overflow. Controls at ≤720: 1 column ✓. Summary at ≤720: 2 columns (each about 50% width) — fine, or at ≤480 1 column. 2 columns at 320px viewport: each card about 140px; the \"Median elapsed time\" label wraps, fine, no horizontal scroll.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: `.summary` at ≤720 is 2 columns — the known-cost note text may wrap; fine.\n\nAlso, `html` should have `lang=\"en\"` ✓ (already there).\n\nMeta description? Not needed.\n\nNow let me write the files. Order: run-explorer.mjs, index.html, styles.css, student-tests.mjs. Then run the exact node --test command.\n\nOne more detail about the mjs — the original file ends with a comment line about implementing browser rendering. I'll restructure the whole file but keep sampleRuns identical (byte-for-byte identical to avoid breaking the \"keep the provided sampleRuns records\" rule).\n\nLet me confirm I keep sampleRuns exactly (lines 1–56).\n\nAbout the code style in this repo: T2 uses JSDoc comments and 2-space indent, semicolons, double quotes. ESLint config — let me peek at eslint.config.mjs to check which rules apply (e.g., `no-unused-vars`, stylistic rules like quotes). Let me read it.\n","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_02f9f5de8001WysT6rtHuDLo0r","sessionID":"ses_fd06f755cffevoqtwk45u3vUdj","messageID":"msg_02f9a1c0d001qYSL61Ano5Uhzx"}}
